  "query_preview": "..A small closed low is currently moving through\nsouthern Arizona into Sonora. This low has kicked off scattered\nshowers and thunderstorms since this morning with the bulk of\nthe activity east of Tucson. Current radar shows isolated\nshowers with occasional lightning strikes east of Tucson mainly\nin Cochise County. The low will continue southward today then\nopen up and move eastward Sunday into early next week. CAMs \nshow continued isolated light to moderate shower activity \nthrough mid-morning mainly in Cochise County, with showers \ndissipating by the afternoon as upper level support wanes. At \nthe same time a surface pressure gradient sets up leading to \nbreezy easterly winds this morning into Sunday. Expect wind \nspeeds of 12-20 mph and gusts to 30 mph, with winds a bit \nstronger in areas open to easterly flow.\n\nBy Monday the low will be an open wave and moving through Texas\nwith another weak shortwave trailing it in Sonora and\nChihuahua. Tuesday into Thursday ridging will be in place\nleading to temperatures warming to around normal for the work\nweek. Friday into the weekend the ridge breaks down and\nensembles favor a more progressive pattern. Ensembles show a\npossible closed low moving into California or Baja Friday into\nSaturday followed by another low digging south from the Pacific\nNorthwest. It's possible next weekend could be on the wet side,\nbut for now NBM PoPs are 15-25 percent late Friday into \nSaturday.",
